  "result": "Perfect! Voucher functionality is fully implemented and working correctly. Here's a summary of what was added:\n\n**New functionality:**\n\n1. **`applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })`** in `src/invoices.js`:\n   - Applies a fixed-amount voucher to a draft invoice\n   - Sets `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n   - Returns `ok(newInvoice)` on success\n   - **Validations**:\n     - Draft invoices only (error: NOT_DRAFT)\n     - One voucher per invoice (error: VOUCHER_EXISTS)\n     - Amount must be positive integer in cents (error: AMOUNT_INVALID)\n   - Does not mutate the original invoice\n\n2. **Updated `invoiceTotals()`**:\n   - Now includes `voucher` field in calculations\n   - Total formula: `subtotal - discount + vat - voucher`\n   - Voucher applied **after** VAT (as per specification)\n   - Returns `voucher: 0` when no voucher applied\n   - Handles edge cases (voucher exceeding total, etc.)\n\n3. **Updated `src/errors.js`**:\n   - Added `VOUCHER_EXISTS` error code\n\n4. **Comprehensive tests** (15 new tests):\n   - Basic voucher application\n   - Immutability verification\n   - Status validation (draft-only)\n   - Amount validation (positive integer)\n   - Single voucher per invoice enforcement\n   - Integration with invoiceTotals\n   - Edge cases (large vouchers, vouchers exceeding total)\n   - Data preservation through applyVoucher\n\nAll 202 tests pass. The voucher is correctly subtracted from the total after VAT calculations, as demonstrated in the example where a \u20ac50 voucher reduced the total from \u20ac1,028.50 to \u20ac978.50.",
